Day 07: Ownership & Special Bits

Phase 2 - Permissions, Ownership & Security | Day 7 of 30

Refer to [commands.md](https://github.com/MideSamuels/OlamideSammy-linux-command-mastery-challenge/blob/main/day-07-ownership/commands.md) for the 10 commands practiced today, including their syntax and my own explanation of what each command does and when I would use it.

What I practiced

I practiced managing file ownership, group ownership, special permissions, and ACLs in Linux. I also worked with SUID, SGID, and the sticky bit, and used commands to inspect and modify access permissions.

What surprised me

I found it interesting that special permission bits can change how files and directories behave. Understanding SGID, SUID, and the sticky bit gave me a better understanding of Linux access control and shared environments.

